1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,960
Good morning.

2
00:00:00,960 --> 00:00:01,940
How can I help you?

3
00:00:01,940 --> 00:00:01,990
Hello.

4
00:00:01,990 --> 00:00:05,900
I'm interested in renting a house somewhere in the town.

5
00:00:05,900 --> 00:00:06,343
Right.

6
00:00:06,343 --> 00:00:09,000
Could I have your name please?

7
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:10,920
Yes, it's Steven Godfrey.

8
00:00:10,920 --> 00:00:14,960
And tell me how many bedrooms you're looking for.

9
00:00:14,960 --> 00:00:16,380
Well, we'd need four,

10
00:00:16,380 --> 00:00:19,930
because I'm going to share the house with three friends.

11
00:00:19,930 --> 00:00:23,540
Okay, there are several of that size on our books.

12
00:00:23,540 --> 00:00:26,760
They mostly belong to families who are working abroad at the moment.

13
00:00:26,760 --> 00:00:28,850
What about the location?

14
00:00:28,850 --> 00:00:31,400
It'd be nice to be central.

15
00:00:31,400 --> 00:00:35,920
That might be difficult, as most houses of that size are in the suburbs.

16
00:00:35,920 --> 00:00:37,937
Still, there are a few.

17
00:00:37,937 --> 00:00:40,760
What's your upper limit for the rent?

18
00:00:40,760 --> 00:00:43,295
We'd like something around ￡500 a month,

19
00:00:43,295 --> 00:00:47,278
but we could go up to ￡600 if we have to.

20
00:00:47,278 --> 00:00:49,450
But we can't go beyond that.

21
00:00:49,450 --> 00:00:53,400
Do you know how long you want to rent the house for?

22
00:00:53,400 --> 00:00:56,310
The minimum let is six months, as you probably realise.

23
00:00:56,310 --> 00:00:58,151
We're at college here for two years,

24
00:00:58,151 --> 00:01:01,834
and we don't want to have to move during that time if we can

25
00:01:01,834 --> 00:01:02,360
avoid it.

26
00:01:02,360 --> 00:01:02,661
Right.

27
00:01:02,661 --> 00:01:05,370
And how soon do you want to move in?

28
00:01:05,370 --> 00:01:08,380
All our lets start on the first of the month.

29
00:01:08,380 --> 00:01:10,900
Well, as soon as possible, really,

30
00:01:10,900 --> 00:01:13,000
so that means September 1st.

31
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:16,528
Okay, let me have a look at what we've got We have photographs of

32
00:01:16,528 --> 00:01:18,040
all the houses on our books,

33
00:01:18,040 --> 00:01:20,560
so you can get an idea of what they're like.

34
00:01:20,560 --> 00:01:25,425
There's this one in Oakington Avenue, at ?550 a month.

35
00:01:25,425 --> 00:01:30,290
Combined living room and dining room, with a separate kitchen.

36
00:01:30,290 --> 00:01:33,930
It doesn't have a garage, though you can park in the road.

37
00:01:33,930 --> 00:01:36,920
Ah, we'd prefer to have one, if possible.

38
00:01:36,920 --> 00:01:37,369
Right.

39
00:01:37,369 --> 00:01:41,860
Then have a look at this house, in Mead Street.

40
00:01:41,860 --> 00:01:46,200
It's got a very large living room and kitchen, bathroom, cloakroom...

41
00:01:46,200 --> 00:01:46,850
How much is it?

42
00:01:46,850 --> 00:01:48,460
That one's 580.

43
00:01:48,460 --> 00:01:51,680
It's very well furnished and equipped.

44
00:01:51,680 --> 00:01:54,202
It also has plenty of space for parking,

45
00:01:54,202 --> 00:01:57,039
and it's available for a minimum of a year.

46
00:01:57,039 --> 00:01:57,354
Oh,

47
00:01:57,354 --> 00:01:58,930
and there's a big garden.

48
00:01:58,930 --> 00:02:01,709
I don't think we could cope with that, to be honest.

49
00:02:01,709 --> 00:02:03,730
We'll be too busy to look after it.

50
00:02:03,730 --> 00:02:04,252
Okay.

51
00:02:04,252 --> 00:02:08,423
Then there's this older house in Hamilton Road:

52
00:02:08,423 --> 00:02:09,988
living room, kitchen-diner,

53
00:02:09,988 --> 00:02:12,596
and it has a study.

54
00:02:12,596 --> 00:02:14,160
550 a month.

55
00:02:14,160 --> 00:02:15,956
That looks rather nice.

56
00:02:15,956 --> 00:02:18,200
But whereabouts in Hamilton Road?

57
00:02:18,200 --> 00:02:20,270
Towards the western end.

58
00:02:20,270 --> 00:02:20,619
Oh,

59
00:02:20,619 --> 00:02:22,014
that'll be very noisy.

60
00:02:22,014 --> 00:02:23,410
I know the area.

61
00:02:23,410 --> 00:02:25,321
Yes, it's pretty lively.

62
00:02:25,321 --> 00:02:27,709
Some people like it, though.

63
00:02:27,709 --> 00:02:31,530
Well, what about this house in Devon Close?

64
00:02:31,530 --> 00:02:33,030
That looks lovely.

65
00:02:33,030 --> 00:02:35,466
There's a big demand for houses in that area,

66
00:02:35,466 --> 00:02:37,360
so prices tend to be quite high.

67
00:02:37,360 --> 00:02:39,710
But this one hasn't been decorated for a few years,

68
00:02:39,710 --> 00:02:41,590
which has kept the rent down a bit.

69
00:02:41,590 --> 00:02:45,438
It's got a living room, dining room and small kitchen,

70
00:02:45,438 --> 00:02:47,362
and it's 595 a month.

71
00:02:47,362 --> 00:02:51,210
I think it would suit you, from what you've said.

72
00:02:51,210 --> 00:02:52,710
It sounds fine.

73
00:02:52,710 --> 00:02:55,750
Why's that part of town so popular?

74
00:02:55,750 --> 00:02:58,284
Well, there's a big scheme to improve the district,

75
00:02:58,284 --> 00:03:01,100
and it'll soon have the best facilities for miles around.

76
00:03:01,100 --> 00:03:02,290
What sort of thing?

77
00:03:02,290 --> 00:03:04,381
There's a big sports centre under construction,

78
00:03:04,381 --> 00:03:06,770
which will be very impressive when it's finished.

79
00:03:06,770 --> 00:03:10,111
In fact the swimming pool's already opened, ahead of schedule,

80
00:03:10,111 --> 00:03:12,450
and it's attracting a lot of people.

81
00:03:12,450 --> 00:03:13,473
What about cinemas:

82
00:03:13,473 --> 00:03:15,520
are there any in the area?

83
00:03:15,520 --> 00:03:17,494
The only one closed down last year,

84
00:03:17,494 --> 00:03:21,160
and it's now in the process of being converted into a film museum.

85
00:03:21,160 --> 00:03:24,970
The local people are trying to get a new cinema added to the scheme.

86
00:03:24,970 --> 00:03:29,528
I think I heard something about a plan to replace the existing concert hall

87
00:03:29,528 --> 00:03:30,830
with a larger one.

88
00:03:30,830 --> 00:03:31,230
Ah,

89
00:03:31,230 --> 00:03:33,630
that's due to start next year.

90
00:03:33,630 --> 00:03:36,113
Well it sounds an interesting area to live in.

91
00:03:36,113 --> 00:03:38,320
Could I go and see the house, please?

92
00:03:38,320 --> 00:03:39,200
Yes, of course.
